From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Madej <lukasz.madej.prv@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bcmdhd: disable DHD_WOWL_IN_SUSPEND_SDIO

The BCM DHD driver gates DHD_WOWL_IN_SUSPEND_SDIO on the absence of
CONFIG_ANDROID_VENDOR_OEM_DATA, so it is unconditionally enabled on
Yocto. With the flag enabled, dhd_pm_callback() on PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE
pushes "wowl", "wowl_activate" and "hostsleep" iovars to the firmware,
followed by an unconditional 1 s msleep meant to let the firmware
settle.

That works when WiFi is associated to an AP. With no AP, wowl_activate
fails and clutters dmesg on every suspend:

  dhd_set_wowl_active: force wowl suspend setting
  dhd_set_wowl_active wowl_activate failed -1

The 1 s msleep is paid either way.

Wake-on-WLAN is not a use case on this board (suspend is driven from
local input, RTC or GPIO, not from network packets). Drop the flag so
dhd_pm_callback() becomes a no-op for SDIO suspend.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Madej <lukasz.madej.prv@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/Makefile | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/Makefile b/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/Makefile
--- a/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/Makefile
@@ -630,8 +630,10 @@ ifneq ($(CONFIG_BCMDHD_PCIE),)
   DHDCFLAGS += -DLIMIT_BORROW
   DHDCFLAGS += -DBULK_DEQUEUE

+# WoWL is unused on this board (no Wake-on-WLAN use case) and only adds a 1 s
+# msleep on every suspend plus "wowl_activate failed -1" spam when no AP.
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_ANDROID_VENDOR_OEM_DATA),)
-  DHDCFLAGS += -DDHD_WOWL_IN_SUSPEND_SDIO
+  # DHDCFLAGS += -DDHD_WOWL_IN_SUSPEND_SDIO
 endif

 # Secure Boot
--
2.43.0
